{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[F]When I jumped off, I had a bucket full of thoughts
[F]When I first jumped off, I held that bucket in [Bb]my hand[Ab]
[F]Ideas that would take me all around the world
[Bb]I stood and watched the smoke behind the [Ab]mountain curl
[Eb]It took me a long time to [Bb]get back on the [F]train
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
Now I'm gone and I'll never look back again
I'm gone and I'll never look back at all
You know I'll never look back again
I turn my face into the howlin' wind
It took me a long time to get back on the train
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
